# Testing and Quality Assurance Standards

## Testing Philosophy

### Test-Driven Approach
- Write tests for all critical business logic
- Test edge cases and error scenarios comprehensively
- Maintain high test coverage for core functionality
- Use tests as documentation for expected behavior
- Ensure tests are reliable and deterministic

### Quality Gates
- All tests must pass before deployment
- Code coverage thresholds must be maintained
- Performance benchmarks must not regress
- Security scans must pass without critical issues
- Accessibility audits must meet WCAG standards

## Testing Strategy

### Unit Testing
- Test individual functions and components in isolation
- Mock external dependencies and API calls
- Use proper test data and fixtures
- Test both success and failure paths
- Validate input/output transformations

### Integration Testing
- Test component interactions and data flow
- Verify API endpoints with real or mock servers
- Test database operations with test databases
- Validate authentication and authorization flows
- Test file upload and processing workflows

### End-to-End Testing
- Test complete user workflows and scenarios
- Validate critical business processes
- Test across different browsers and devices
- Verify responsive design implementations
- Test accessibility with screen readers

### Performance Testing
- Benchmark critical operations and APIs
- Test load handling and concurrent users
- Validate database query performance
- Monitor bundle size and load times
- Test memory usage and potential leaks

## Implementation Guidelines

### Frontend Testing
```typescript
// ✅ Component testing with proper setup
import { render, screen, fireEvent, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react';
import { vi } from 'vitest';
import UserForm from './UserForm';

describe('UserForm', () => {
  const mockOnSubmit = vi.fn();
  
  beforeEach(() => {
    mockOnSubmit.mockClear();
  });

  it('submits valid user data', async () => {
    render(<UserForm onSubmit={mockOnSubmit} />);
    
    await fireEvent.change(screen.getByLabelText('Email'), {
      target: { value: 'test@example.com' }
    });
    
    await fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit' }));
    
    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(mockOnSubmit).toHaveBeenCalledWith({
        email: 'test@example.com'
      });
    });
  });

  it('displays validation errors for invalid data', async () => {
    render(<UserForm onSubmit={mockOnSubmit} />);
    
    await fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit' }));
    
    expect(screen.getByText('Email is required')).toBeInTheDocument();
    expect(mockOnSubmit).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
  });
});
```

### API Testing
```typescript
// ✅ API route testing
import { NextRequest } from 'next/server';
import { POST } from './route';

describe('/api/users', () => {
  it('creates user with valid data', async () => {
    const request = new NextRequest('http://localhost:3000/api/users', {
      method: 'POST',
      body: JSON.stringify({
        email: 'test@example.com',
        name: 'Test User'
      }),
      headers: {
        'content-type': 'application/json'
      }
    });

    const response = await POST(request);
    const data = await response.json();

    expect(response.status).toBe(201);
    expect(data).toHaveProperty('id');
    expect(data.email).toBe('test@example.com');
  });

  it('validates required fields', async () => {
    const request = new NextRequest('http://localhost:3000/api/users', {
      method: 'POST',
      body: JSON.stringify({}),
      headers: {
        'content-type': 'application/json'
      }
    });

    const response = await POST(request);
    const data = await response.json();

    expect(response.status).toBe(400);
    expect(data).toHaveProperty('error');
  });
});
```

### Database Testing
```typescript
// ✅ Database operation testing
import { createTestClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js';
import { userService } from './userService';

describe('UserService', () => {
  let testDb: any;

  beforeAll(async () => {
    testDb = createTestClient(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL);
    await testDb.from('users').delete().match({});
  });

  afterEach(async () => {
    await testDb.from('users').delete().match({});
  });

  it('creates user with valid data', async () => {
    const userData = {
      email: 'test@example.com',
      name: 'Test User'
    };

    const user = await userService.create(userData);

    expect(user).toHaveProperty('id');
    expect(user.email).toBe(userData.email);

    const dbUser = await testDb
      .from('users')
      .select('*')
      .eq('id', user.id)
      .single();

    expect(dbUser.data).toBeTruthy();
  });
});
```

## Quality Assurance Practices

### Code Review Requirements
- All code must be reviewed by at least one other developer
- Tests must be included with new features and bug fixes
- Security implications must be considered and documented
- Performance impact must be assessed
- Documentation must be updated for public APIs

### Automated Quality Checks
- TypeScript compilation without errors
- ESLint and Biome formatting compliance
- Automated security vulnerability scanning
- Dependency audit and update checks
- Bundle size analysis and optimization

### Accessibility Testing
- Keyboard navigation testing
- Screen reader compatibility
- Color contrast validation
- Focus management verification
- ARIA attributes implementation

### Browser and Device Testing
- Cross-browser compatibility (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)
- Mobile responsiveness on various screen sizes
- Touch interaction testing
- Performance on slower devices
- Offline functionality where applicable

## Test Data Management

### Test Fixtures
- Use consistent test data across test suites
- Create reusable test factories and builders
- Implement proper test data cleanup
- Use database transactions for test isolation
- Mock external services consistently

### Environment Setup
```typescript
// ✅ Test environment configuration
export const testConfig = {
  database: {
    url: process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL,
    reset: true
  },
  auth: {
    testUser: {
      email: 'test@example.com',
      password: 'testpassword'
    }
  },
  storage: {
    bucket: 'test-uploads'
  }
};

export const setupTestEnvironment = async () => {
  // Reset test database
  await resetTestDatabase();
  
  // Clear test storage
  await clearTestStorage();
  
  // Setup test user
  await createTestUser();
};
```

### Mock Strategies
- Mock external API calls and services
- Use dependency injection for testability
- Create realistic mock data
- Implement proper error simulation
- Test timeout and retry scenarios

## Performance and Load Testing

### Performance Benchmarks
```typescript
// ✅ Performance testing
import { performance } from 'perf_hooks';

describe('Performance Tests', () => {
  it('processes large datasets efficiently', async () => {
    const startTime = performance.now();
    
    const result = await processLargeDataset(generateTestData(10000));
    
    const endTime = performance.now();
    const duration = endTime - startTime;
    
    expect(duration).toBeLessThan(1000); // Should complete within 1 second
    expect(result).toHaveLength(10000);
  });

  it('handles concurrent requests', async () => {
    const requests = Array(100).fill(null).map(() => 
      fetch('/api/users', { method: 'GET' })
    );
    
    const responses = await Promise.all(requests);
    
    responses.forEach(response => {
      expect(response.status).toBe(200);
    });
  });
});
```

### Load Testing
- Test API endpoints under realistic load
- Validate database performance with concurrent connections
- Test file upload limits and timeouts
- Monitor memory usage during stress tests
- Validate error handling under load

## Continuous Integration

### Automated Testing Pipeline
1. Unit tests execution
2. Integration tests with test database
3. End-to-end tests in staging environment
4. Performance benchmark validation
5. Security vulnerability scanning
6. Bundle size analysis
7. Accessibility audit

### Quality Gates
- Minimum 80% code coverage for new code
- All tests must pass
- No critical security vulnerabilities
- Performance benchmarks within acceptable range
- Bundle size within limits
- Accessibility score above minimum threshold

## Testing Anti-Patterns to Avoid

- ❌ Testing implementation details instead of behavior
- ❌ Writing tests that depend on external services without mocking
- ❌ Creating flaky tests that pass/fail randomly
- ❌ Not testing error conditions and edge cases
- ❌ Using production data in tests
- ❌ Writing tests that test the framework instead of your code
- ❌ Having tests that are slow and block development
- ❌ Not maintaining tests when requirements change
- ❌ Testing everything through the UI instead of unit tests
- ❌ Not cleaning up test data and resources

## Documentation and Reporting

### Test Documentation
- Document test scenarios and expected outcomes
- Maintain test data requirements and setup instructions
- Document known issues and workarounds
- Keep performance benchmark history
- Document testing environment setup

### Quality Metrics
- Track test coverage trends over time
- Monitor test execution times and flakiness
- Report on security scan results
- Track performance benchmark results
- Monitor accessibility compliance scores
